-- title:
--   Rejected effects vanish on every forward non-loop edge
-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Background.Introspection.HonestPauliGame` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). Perfect PCC play of the full Pauli basis game. All question types use the actual honest field-register measurements and a single extra qubit. The sampler's support supplies one common content for both questions; every graph edge is handled, including its reverse and every self-loop. Wrong-format answers retain zero effects throughout.
--
--   Rejected effects vanish on every forward non-loop edge.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open MIPRE
--   open MIPRE.QLD
--   open MIPRE.QLD.Honest
--   open Matrix Finset MIPRE.Weyl MIPRE.LCS MIPRE.Introspection Classical
--   variable {F : Type*} [Field F] [Fintype F] [DecidableEq F] [Algebra (ZMod 2) F]
--
--   theorem MIPRE.QLD.Honest.answerOp_adjRaw_reject (hm : m ∣ Fintype.card F) (hd : 1 ≤ d)
--       (c : Content F m) (t u : Ty) (h : adjRaw t u = true) (a b : Answer F m d)
--       (hr : accepts hm (c.question hm t) (c.question hm u) a b = false) :
--       answerOp hm (c.question hm t) a * answerOp hm (c.question hm u) b = 0
